# Core Standards

- **Style & consistency**
  - Prefer clear, descriptive names over abbreviations.
  - Keep functions and components focused; extract helpers when logic grows.
  - Avoid unnecessary comments; comments should explain why, not what.

- **Nullability & errors**
  - Narrow null and undefined as early as possible instead of relying on deep optional chains.
  - Fail fast with helpful errors and messages; avoid swallowing errors silently.

- **Testing & safety**
  - When changing core logic, prefer adding or updating tests rather than doing manual-only verification.
  - Log in a structured, consistent way on the server; avoid noisy console logging in committed code.

- **Project hygiene**
  - Do not commit generated files, local logs, or environment secrets.
  - Keep TODO notes actionable and dated, or create an issue instead.
